requirement:
The FastAPI project below (entry point `app.main:app`) has a bug. Fix it so the behaviour described in SPEC holds, keep every existing endpoint/function and its signature, and return the COMPLETE corrected project including its unit tests (add a test that would have caught the bug).

SYMPTOM: `Ann@Example.com` and `ann@example.com` can both be registered, so one person gets two accounts; lookups are also case-sensitive.

SPEC: Emails are case-insensitive and whitespace around them is ignored: they are stored and returned lower-cased and stripped, a duplicate (ignoring case/whitespace) returns 409, and `GET /users/{email}` finds the user regardless of case.

Existing project files:

File `app/main.py`:
```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException
from pydantic import BaseModel

app = FastAPI()
USERS: dict[str, dict] = {}


class NewUser(BaseModel):
    email: str
    name: str


@app.post("/users", status_code=201)
def create(u: NewUser):
    if u.email in USERS:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail="exists")
    USERS[u.email] = {"email": u.email, "name": u.name}
    return USERS[u.email]


@app.get("/users/{email}")
def get(email: str):
    if email not in USERS:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="not found")
    return USERS[email]
```
